dinero-core (8.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * v8.1.1 — CONSENSUS RELEASE. Activates OP_CHECKTEMPLATEVERIFY (BIP-119)
    and OP_CHECKCONTRACTVERIFY together at mainnet block 100,000. The daemon
    is NOT byte-identical to v8.0.18 and a full fleet redeploy IS required:
    every validating and mining node must run this release before block
    99,000, the go/no-go checkpoint. A node still on v8.0.18 at block 100,000
    will split from the network.
    .
    Both opcodes are bound to a single constant
    (MAINNET_COVENANT_PROFILE_V1_HEIGHT) so neither can activate without the
    other. OP_CHECKSIGFROMSTACK and OP_TXHASH remain dormant (UINT32_MAX).
    Consensus checksum changes to
    68e0a99766e8ab1224ee040ec715bbbd0a544a59d4b3a96025dd35f77f4e960a.
    .
    Deploying this release does NOT activate the opcodes: they stay dormant
    until block 100,000 regardless of when the binary is installed. Public
    review runs over the block window [78,245 -> 99,000] (issue #503).
    .
    Assurance evidence, reproducible from a clean checkout: full upstream
    BIP-119 vector corpus, CCV adversarial suite, an implementation-independent
    CCV reference model differentially tested against production, mutation
    coverage proving every normative CCV clause is load-bearing, sanitizer
    fuzzing over the live Taproot path, and bounded-state exhaustive
    enumeration. No paid external audit was obtained; that residual risk is
    recorded explicitly rather than glossed over.
    .
    Also in this release:
    - SelectParams() now validates chain parameters before publishing them,
      so a rejected chain can no longer leave the process reporting
      parameters consensus refused (PR #499).
    - Test-integrity repairs: assert() is compiled out under NDEBUG, which
      CI uses, so assert-only tests were passing without checking anything.
      This had been hiding a stale premine model in the monetary tests --
      Dinero has no premine. Converted, and a CI ratchet now blocks new raw
      assertions (PR #498, issue #497).
    - Fail-closed AssumeUTXO snapshot format policy: V2 deprecated
      unconditionally, V3 rejected at or after shielded activation (PR #496).
    - Registered the shipped 73,035 v4 trust anchor (PR #495).

