dinero-core (8.0.16-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * v8.0.16 — Utreexo write-reduction + snapshot-bootstrap fixes (non-consensus;
    no rule or activation changes; safe to upgrade any time). Highlights:
    - CSN/stateless reorg convergence: ActivateBestChain-owned atomic reorg,
      fixing the pre-existing CSN reorg-convergence failures.
    - Every-N forest-checkpoint write reduction: a full Utreexo forest
      checkpoint every N blocks (utreexo.checkpoint_interval, default 500) with
      reversible per-block UD delta sidecars between anchors; restore replays
      nearest checkpoint + deltas (header-verified per block). ~N-fold reduction
      in checkpoint write volume on both full-node and CSN/mobile paths.
    - AssumeUTXO snapshot bootstrap: genesis UTXO is preserved until a snapshot
      passes every preflight (transport/manifest/checksum/consensus), so a
      rejected snapshot can no longer strand the node in the unrecoverable
      consensus-utxo-tip invariant loop; the genesis-only precondition is now
      content-based (fixes deferred mobile bootstrap where tip height > 0).
    - Mainnet snapshot pipeline: generate_snapshot.sh passes -datadir and dumps
      inside the daemon datadir (no systemd PrivateTmp isolation, no missing RPC
      cookie).
    - iOS embedded hardening, forest deserialize all-or-nothing, stateless
      missing-proof reject, installer-time fresh-snapshot fetch, quiet logging.

 -- DineroLabs <team@dinerolabs.org>  Sat, 18 Jul 2026 06:57:01 +0000

dinero-core (8.0.15-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * v8.0.15 — AssumeUTXO stability + memory-safety release (non-consensus; no
    rule or activation changes). HIGH PRIORITY: fixes a memory-corruption bug
    on nodes that fast-sync from an AssumeUTXO snapshot. Safe to upgrade any
    time; recommended for all snapshot-bootstrapping nodes (embedded/mobile
    wallets and fresh desktop installs).
    - chainstate: fix a data race on the unreadable-blocks set. It was cleared
      from the scheduler-drain/peer thread while inserted/read under
      activation_mutex_ on other threads — concurrent std::unordered_set
      mutation (undefined behavior) that corrupted process-wide heap, surfacing
      as false utreexo-root mismatches in the isolated background-validation
      thread and a SIGSEGV in an unrelated thread. Encapsulated in a
      self-synchronizing UnreadableBlockSet with a leaf mutex; added a
      concurrency regression test (TSAN-gated in CI).
    - qt: pass --assumeutxo_forward_connect on fresh installs that bootstrap
      from the bundled snapshot, so the wallet is usable at the live tip within
      minutes instead of showing received funds as 0-confirmations for the
      whole genesis→base background validation window.
    - assumeutxo: don't escalate a transient replay body-read failure to a
      permanent fatal_mismatch. Verify the body's merkle root on read and
      require a validation failure to reproduce on a fresh pass before
      declaring the snapshot fatal (spec #298 fatal semantics preserved for
      confirmed mismatches).
    - consensus: fix a remotely-triggerable out-of-bounds read in
      UtreexoProof::deserialize (numSiblings*32 computed in 32-bit arithmetic
      wrapped the length guard); now uses checked size_t arithmetic.

