dinero-core (8.0.0~rc1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First unified release from the DineroLabs/dinero monorepo (formerly
    DineroLabs/Dinero-Coin + DineroLabs/dinero-qt + DineroLabs/dinero-solo-miner).
    One source tree, one tag, one version string — daemon, CLI, Qt GUI, solo
    miner all derive from the same commit.
  * Mining backend stack: dinero-solo-miner gains a MinerBackend enum with
    --backend <auto|cpu|metal|cuda|opencl> CLI selection. CUDA + Metal +
    OpenCL backends use runtime kernel compilation (NVRTC / clBuildProgram /
    MTLLibrary newLibraryWithSource) — no nvcc at build time, sidestepping
    the CUDA 12.2 + MSVC 14.44 toolchain mismatch. CPU-verify-before-submit
    catches any GPU-backend hash divergence at runtime.
  * Peer discovery: full propagation stack now wired end-to-end. handle_addr
    forwards new addresses to 2 random outbound peers (Bitcoin Core fanout);
    keepalive_loop re-sends getaddr every 24h; peers.dat write is atomic
    (.tmp + fsync + rename) with periodic + on-shutdown saves; per-release
    fixed-seeds generator (contrib/seeds/generate-seeds.py) produces
    include/consensus/chainparamsseeds.h from a curated input; new
    dinero-seeder binary auto-curates seeds_main.txt candidates from
    observed network reachability.
  * .deb contract unchanged: dinero-core ships dinerod + dinero-cli only,
    no GPU mining, no hardware-wallet HID stack, no gRPC runtime surface,
    no auto-enable or auto-start in postinst. Operators wanting GPU mining
    or the Qt GUI install separate packages.

