dinero-core (2.2.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial .deb skeleton (Phase E.1 of Dinero Core 1.0).
  * Ships dinerod, dinero-cli, dinero-backup, dinero-prepare-upgrade
    and the auxiliary mining binaries to /usr/bin/.
  * Ships dinero.conf example, dinero.service example, and a
    journald retention drop-in example at /usr/share/doc/dinero/.
  * Ships the active systemd unit at /lib/systemd/system/dinero.service
    (NOT auto-enabled — operator runs `systemctl enable --now dinero`).
  * Postinst creates the `dinero` system user and the
    /var/lib/dinero/ datadir at mode 0750.
  * Postrm on `purge` removes /var/lib/dinero/, /etc/dinero/, and
    the dinero user. On `remove` (non-purge) preserves them so
    chain data and wallet seeds are not lost on a routine package
    removal.
  * Dependency surface is system-linked. Phase E.3 bundles
    librocksdb / libgrpc / libprotobuf / libabsl etc. under
    /usr/lib/dinero/ via DT_RUNPATH, narrowing Depends: to
    base-system libraries only.

